WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:05.926
Gravity is always present. To hover, upward force must at least balance the vehicle’s

2
00:00:06.001 --> 00:00:09.536
weight. To climb, force must exceed it.

3
00:00:09.786 --> 00:00:12.661
But acceleration alone is not enough.

4
00:00:12.736 --> 00:00:15.314
A vehicle must also remain stable.

5
00:00:15.738 --> 00:00:20.938
A nozzle mounted away from the center of mass can spin the machine even when the total

6
00:00:21.038 --> 00:00:28.113
force looks manageable. Flight is a continuous negotiation between forces, moments,

7
00:00:28.188 --> 00:00:29.910
energy, and control.

8
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.845
Near Earth, the gravitational force on a vehicle is its mass multiplied by roughly

9
00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:39.420
nine point eight one meters per second squared.

10
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.795
A thousand-kilogram aircraft weighs about nine point eight kilonewtons.

11
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:50.793
To hold altitude without vertical acceleration, upward force must balance that weight.

12
00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.857
To climb, extra net upward force is required.

13
00:00:54.982 --> 00:01:00.137
Force changes linear momentum. Torque changes angular momentum.

14
00:01:00.422 --> 00:01:03.472
A flying machine needs to control both.

15
00:01:03.547 --> 00:01:06.147
Pitch tips the nose up or down.

16
00:01:06.247 --> 00:01:09.334
Roll banks the vehicle. Yaw changes heading.

17
00:01:09.781 --> 00:01:14.631
An uncontrolled pitch moment could destabilize the aircraft even if its average upward

18
00:01:14.706 --> 00:01:21.306
thrust matches its weight. A rotor generates thrust by accelerating a large mass of

19
00:01:21.356 --> 00:01:27.856
air downward. Ideal momentum theory tells us that the power for hover increases faster

20
00:01:27.981 --> 00:01:30.487
than linearly with the needed thrust.

21
00:01:31.081 --> 00:01:36.656
Increasing effective rotor disk area reduces ideal induced power.

22
00:01:36.781 --> 00:01:42.556
Real rotor drag, efficiency, structure and flight conditions make actual power

23
00:01:42.606 --> 00:01:43.957
requirements higher.
